cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Quantum Projection: amplitude-encoded statevectors projected onto a stored subspace (SYNTHETIC classical emulation)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/quantum-projection"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC. Standard-library Python classical emulation of quantum
  kinematics: amplitude-encoded statevectors stored in a complex
  outer-product memory, overlap-based projection onto the stored subspace,
  and lossy Haar coarse-graining (equivalent to projecting one qubit onto
  |+>). With orthonormal patterns the memory is a projector and recall
  reaches its fixed point in one step; with non-orthogonal patterns repeated
  recall drifts to the dominant eigenvector. Includes 200-seed sweeps with
  unstored and random controls. No speedup, no Bell violation, no hardware
  data.
keywords:
  - "quantum-kinematics"
  - "statevector"
  - "holographic-memory"
  - "complex-hopfield"
  - "born-rule"
  - "coarse-graining"
  - "synthetic"
  - "python"
